    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Kalashtar Classes (Customizable Origins)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-custom-origin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-custom-origin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re using the option “"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Customizing Your Origin",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/tcoe/character-options#CustomizingYourOrigin"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything. If you’re not using those rules, scroll down to the next section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Between spells and infusions, artificers are generally very durable, but they\n\tdon’t have good Wisdom saves and they don’t have a way to get resistance to\n\tpsychic damage. The Kalashtar’s additional defenses patch those\n\tvulnerabilities.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Barbarians have poor Wisdom saves, and the conditions which target Wisdom\n\tsaves are typically very problematic for barbarians. Advantage on those saves\n\tprovides a significant defensive benefit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-barbarian-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Path of the Totem (Bear) offers resistance to every damage type except\n\tpsychic, so the Kalashtar neatly fits in to fill that defensive gap, making\n\tbear totem absurdly difficult to kill."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While people generally worry about their front-line martial characters being\n\tfrightened or mind-controlled or whatever, bards are just as vulnerable.\n\tAdvantage on Wisdom saves is a good defensive benefit. Bards can also make\n\texcellent use of the Kalashtar’s telepathy, allowing them to serve as a Face\n\twithout worrying about languages."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Psychic damage is rare and clerics are already great with Wisdom saving\n\tthrows, so the Kalashtar adds very little."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Psychic damage is rare and druids are already great with Wisdom saving throws, so the Kalashtar adds very little. Telepathy appears to work while using Wild Shape, which is a nice convenience, but not enough to make the build especially effective."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fighters have poor Wisdom saves, and the conditions which target Wisdom saves\n\tare typically very problematic for fighters. Advantage on those saves provides\n\ta significant defensive benefit."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Psychic damage is rare and monks are already great with Wisdom saving throws,\n\tso the Kalashtar adds very little."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "One uncommon damage type isn’t a huge problem for the Paladin and their saves\n\tare already great thanks to Aura of Protection and proficiency in Wisdom\n\tsaving throws, so the Kalasthar adds very little to the Paladin."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Despite their partial dependence on Wisdom, rangers’ Wisdom saves still\n\taren’t great so they face the same vulnerabilities as barbarians and\n\tfighters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The ability to communicate telepathically is nice for a class that typically\n\tdepends on remaining undetected, and the Kalasthar’s racial telepathy is the\n\tbest available (there are many telepathic races, almost all of them with\n\tunique telepathy mechanics). Advantage on Wisdom saves coupled with the\n\tRogue’s Evasion provides broad defensive coverage. So as long as your\n\tConstitution saves are decent you’re very resilient."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sorcerers aren’t proficient in Wisdom saves like warlocks and wizards, so\n\tconstant Advantage on those saves is helpful. Otherwise, there’s not much\n\there."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Warlocks are already proficienct in Wisdom saves. Advantage certainly doesn’t\n\thurt, and the Warlock’s saves won’t match a cleric or a druid, but it’s not\n\tuseful enough to make it a great build."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Wizard are already proficienct in Wisdom saves. Advantage certainly doesn’t\n\thurt, and the Wizard’s saves won’t match a cleric or a druid, but it’s not\n\tuseful enough to make it a great build."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Kalashtar Classes (Default Rules)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-default",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-default-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re "
            },
            {
              "type": "emphasis",
              "text": "not"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " using the option “Customizing Your Origin” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything or the updated version of the race published in Mordenkainen’s Monsters of the Multiverse. If you are using those rules, scroll up to the previous section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Intelligence increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Resistance to psychic damage seems really exciting for the Berserker because\n\tyou can have resistance to all damage. Unfortunately, that’s not enough to\n\tmake you a good barbarian."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While the Kalasthar’s Charisma increase isn’t as good as their Wisdom\n\tincrease, +1 is still plenty for any full spellcaster. The Kalashtar’s\n\ttelepathy offers a unique tool, especially for a bard that does a lot of\n\tsneaking, infiltration, or other subterfuge."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Kalashtar’s Wisdom increase and their defensive traits work great for the\n\tCleric. Between high Wisdom, proficiency, and Advantage on Wisdom saving\n\tthrows you’re all but guaranteed to pass Wisdom saves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Kalashtar makes a great druid for the same reasons that they make a great\n\tcleric. Additionally, since their racial traits are all mental rather than\n\tphysical they persist while using Wild Shape. For example: you can use Mind\n\tLink while using Wild Shape, allowing you to communicate effectively without\n\treverting to your normal form."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No increases to physical ability scores."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Wisdom increase helps, but it’s not enough to make you a good monk and\n\tnone of the Kalashtar’s other traits meaningfully support the Monk. This is\n\tprobably the Kalashtar’s best non-spellcaster class option, but it’s still a\n\tvery hard choice, which is unfortunate because thematically I think a\n\tkalashtar monk would be very interesting."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Charisma bonus is not enough on its own. The Paladin is likely the\n\tKalashtar’s best martial class option, but it’s still a bad option."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Without a Strength or Dexterity increase, the Ranger is a really difficult\n\toption. Wisdom adds to your spellcasting, but without an ability increase to\n\tsupport your damage output and Stealth you’ll fall behind on some of the\n\tclass’s biggest functions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Without a Dexterity increase, the Rogue is a difficult option. Still,\n\tTelepathy and a Wisdom increase are an interesting option for rogue subclasses\n\tlike the Inquisitive which emphasize Dexterity-based options less."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While the Kalasthar’s Charisma increase isn’t as good as their Wisdom\n\tincrease, +1 is still plenty for any full spellcaster. Sorcerers don’t tend to\n\tbe stealthy, but you can rely on magical invisibility and telepathy to remain\n\tundetected in combat and still support your allies. If you use Sublte Spell\n\tand spells which don’t make attacks or require saves, you can remain invisible\n\tfor long periods and still be effective by supporting your allies or acting\n\tindirectly."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While the Kalasthar’s Charisma increase isn’t as good as their Wisdom\n\tincrease, +1 is still plenty for any full spellcaster. Telepathy is a neat\n\toption, but warlocks aren’t skill-heavy like the bar so stealth is less of an\n\toption (though it is still an option) and with limited spell slots you can’t\n\tmake invisibility a go-to tactic like the Bard or the Sorcerer could. The\n\tWarlock is still a good option, but it lacks the synergies between racial\n\ttraits and class features which make the Bard a great option."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Wizard",
